focused on seeing the good,

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:14.751
so that's how I see it.

00:10:14.751 --> 00:10:15.870
- That's, you're hardwired
to be optimistic anyway.

00:10:15.870 --> 00:10:17.970
- I do believe that, I do believe that.

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:19.810
But I do think it was encouraged.

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:22.400
I do think that if my
dad and mom switched,

00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:24.868
and I grew up with a parent
that was deeply pessimistic

00:10:24.868 --> 00:10:26.736
from one to 14 that some

00:10:26.736 --> 00:10:31.530
of that optimism would have
gone from an eight to a seven

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:34.530
versus where I think with
my mom an eight to a 10.

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:35.850
So I do think, you know,

00:10:35.850 --> 00:10:38.310
this has been figured out
long before I came along.

00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:41.370
This nature/nurture
environment is very real.

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:43.040
And so yes I think there are things deeply

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:44.960
DNA wise about me,

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:46.870
but I do think the way I was nurtured,

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:48.290
the environment I grew up in

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:49.420
and the parenting I had

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:50.920
had an impact as well.

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:52.335
Much like I look at my sister

00:10:52.335 --> 00:10:54.720
who's only three and a half
years younger than me, right?

00:10:54.720 --> 00:10:57.520
For me, by the way I know
all the noises going on,

00:10:57.520 --> 00:10:58.580
I see everybody behind camera.

00:10:58.580 --> 00:10:59.580
I love this.

00:10:59.580 --> 00:11:00.681
So if you're watching at home,

00:11:00.681 --> 00:11:03.004
I love the chaos so.

00:11:03.004 --> 00:11:04.440
- We're backstage, this is what happens.

00:11:04.440 --> 00:11:06.180
- Um, my sister's only three

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:07.540
and a half years younger than me

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:09.088
and she's wired to be pessimistic.

00:11:09.088 --> 00:11:12.450
And I think she's a three who got parented

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:15.110
and had an older brother
that moved her to a six.

00:11:15.110 --> 00:11:17.331
Again, if she was raised
by my grandmother,

00:11:17.331 --> 00:11:19.870
who was very pessimistic
she might have been a three

00:11:19.870 --> 00:11:21.174
that became a one.

00:11:21.174 --> 00:11:22.840
- Yeah, interesting.
- And so that's how I see it.

00:11:22.840 --> 00:11:23.673
- Yeah.

00:11:23.673 --> 00:11:25.250
Where do you see yourself zero to 10

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:26.480
on the happiness scale?

00:11:26.480 --> 00:11:27.313
- 11.

00:11:27.313 --> 00:11:28.530
- Every day?

00:11:28.530 --> 00:11:29.363
- Every day.

00:11:29.363 --> 00:11:30.440
- Really?

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:31.645
- I'm driven by gratitude.

00:11:31.645 --> 00:11:35.510
I'm incapable of being upset

00:11:35.510 --> 00:11:36.818
around things that don't matter.

00:11:36.818 --> 00:11:41.200
Everything besides the health
of nine people doesn't matter.

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:44.330
When a parent of mine passes away

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:46.210
that 11 will become a zero.

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:47.043
- Yeah, right.

00:11:47.043 --> 00:11:49.950
- For a day, a month,
a year, I don't know.

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:51.441
I haven't crossed that bridge.

00:11:51.441 --> 00:11:56.441
But I have put myself in a
very interesting box mentally,

00:11:56.923 --> 00:12:00.760
which is my perspective is binary.

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:02.220
It is black and white.

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:04.790
Either the nine or 10 or 11 people

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:06.110
I love the most are healthy

00:12:06.110 --> 00:12:07.750
and woke up this morning,

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:11.241
and didn't die and thus
I'm fully happy, or not.

00:12:11.241 --> 00:12:13.148
And losing an account

00:12:13.148 --> 00:12:16.830
or having people write
something bad about me

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:18.048
or having a PR headache,

00:12:18.048 --> 00:12:20.615
or something didn't work
out the way I wanted

00:12:20.615 --> 00:12:23.520
or somebody stabbed me in the back,

00:12:23.520 --> 00:12:26.387
or, it just, it resonates for a second,

00:12:26.387 --> 00:12:28.235
maybe it gets,

00:12:28.235 --> 00:12:30.580
I mean extremely difficult things

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:32.452
that I notice contemporaries struggle with

00:12:32.452 --> 00:12:36.419
carry three minutes of
anxiousness with me,

00:12:36.419 --> 00:12:39.559
65 seconds of inconvenience.

00:12:39.559 --> 00:12:43.853
Me, if it's traumatic
maybe a couple of hours

00:12:43.853 --> 00:12:48.240
before it translates into
this really doesn't matter.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:49.830
- So it's a little,
what you say to yourself

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:50.820
at the time,

00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:52.850
or do you practice (mumbles) over time?

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:54.970
- I probably have spent the last 15 years

00:12:54.970 --> 00:12:57.262
of my life making
pretend that my mom died.

00:12:57.262 --> 00:12:58.389
- (laughing)

00:12:58.389 --> 00:13:00.230
Are you serious?

00:13:00.230 --> 00:13:01.389
- Yeah.

00:13:01.389 --> 00:13:02.222
(laughing)

00:13:02.222 --> 00:13:03.055
Yeah.

00:13:03.055 --> 00:13:04.560
I do a lot of things where
something great happens

00:13:04.560 --> 00:13:05.676
or something bad happens,

00:13:05.676 --> 00:13:08.010
and I make pretend and then the phone rang

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:08.930
and my mom died.

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:10.093
So how would I feel?

00:13:10.093 --> 00:13:12.370
Would I feel like this huge trophy

00:13:12.370 --> 00:13:13.530
I just got meant anything?

00:13:13.530 --> 00:13:14.363
No.

00:13:14.363 --> 00:13:15.900
Would I feel like this terrible

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:17.850
thing that happened in
business today was terrible?

00:13:17.850 --> 00:13:18.730
No.

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:21.452
So, yeah, I've been practicing
for a very long time.

00:13:21.452 --> 00:13:22.362
- That's a really

00:13:22.362 --> 00:13:24.871
massive way to look at things.

00:13:24.871 --> 00:13:25.860
- Yeah.

00:13:25.860 --> 00:13:27.020
- Yeah, I love that.

00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:28.970
- Yeah, it really works for me.

00:13:28.970 --> 00:13:30.210
- I can see how it would work,

00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:32.386
but it's not something
anyone would think of.

00:13:32.386 --> 00:13:34.170
- Yeah it's something
I've been thinking about

00:13:34.170 --> 00:13:35.260
putting out more in the world.

00:13:35.260 --> 00:13:36.490
Like really just think about it.

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:37.840
Like just really wake up

00:13:37.840 --> 00:13:38.950
and go to sleep every night,

00:13:38.950 --> 00:13:41.640
and make pretend the singular
person you love the most

00:13:41.640 --> 00:13:43.250
just died in a horrific accident.

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:44.916
I know it, I get it, I get it.

00:13:44.916 --> 00:13:47.220
But look, I wanna be very empathetic.

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:50.550
People watching this,
we all know the majority

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:52.328
of the world deals with issues.

00:13:52.328 --> 00:13:54.752
Watching a man who just said he's 11 on

00:13:54.752 --> 00:13:56.172
the one to 10 happiness scale,

00:13:56.172 --> 00:13:59.668
that can come across very insincere.

00:13:59.668 --> 00:14:03.098
And the followup to why I'm there

00:14:03.098 --> 00:14:06.888
is an extreme different
kind of thought process

00:14:06.888 --> 00:14:10.100
that isn't talked about
in contemporary times

00:14:10.100 --> 00:14:12.511
that I would like to
argue is worth a debate.

00:14:12.511 --> 00:14:14.700
Whether it works for others or not,

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:15.533
I don't know.

00:14:15.533 --> 00:14:18.160
But it is what I do.

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:19.070
It is what I do.

00:14:19.070 --> 00:14:19.987
And-

00:14:19.987 --> 00:14:21.159
- And-

00:14:21.159 --> 00:14:22.165
- Please.

00:14:22.165 --> 00:14:23.390
- People are seeing you
as seeing so successful

00:14:23.390 --> 00:14:25.090
they wanna know how your brain tics.

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:27.185
So maybe these little things,

00:14:27.185 --> 00:14:28.018
the things we haven't thought about

00:14:28.018 --> 00:14:28.970
that we should be thinking about.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:32.240
- And if they look at
my success as an ability

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:34.426
to walk around very light

00:14:34.426 --> 00:14:36.360
versus the money I've made

00:14:36.360 --> 00:14:37.705
or the followers I have,

00:14:37.705 --> 00:14:42.420
then the hack that I just
gave is even more powerful.

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:43.700
And I would argue that a lot

00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:45.617
of my business success comes from the fact

00:14:45.617 --> 00:14:47.230
that I have not had to take a lot

00:14:47.230 --> 00:14:51.562
of hours ever in 25 professional years

00:14:51.562 --> 00:14:53.600
to sit and worry about something

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:55.410
that's happening outside the business.

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:58.055
I'm giving it my all, care free,

00:14:58.055 --> 00:15:02.173
and that's how I see it.

00:15:02.173 --> 00:15:03.311
- (mumbles) to when you were at school.

00:15:03.311 --> 00:15:06.061
So what was the tricky things
that made you get the D's

00:15:06.061 --> 00:15:07.240
and the F's?

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:08.790
Was it, were you dyslexic?

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:09.623
ADHD?

00:15:09.623 --> 00:15:10.620
- Probably, probably.

00:15:10.620 --> 00:15:11.453
I don't know.

00:15:11.453 --> 00:15:12.300
I wasn't diagnosed with either,

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:13.887
but it was a different time in the '80s.

00:15:13.887 --> 00:15:17.200
It was deep self awareness

00:15:17.200 --> 00:15:18.988
that everything that was
going on in that classroom

00:15:18.988 --> 00:15:21.550
was completely irrelevant to what

00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:22.800
I was going to be.

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:23.633
- Yeah.

00:15:23.633 --> 00:15:27.481
- It was either a mix
of unbelievable audacity

00:15:27.481 --> 00:15:31.817
or incredible self awareness
at such a young age,

00:15:31.817 --> 00:15:34.330
and probably a little bit of both.

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:37.300
And I just remember being in fourth grade.

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:40.804
I remember vividly sitting
in Mr. Momar's science class

00:15:40.804 --> 00:15:44.990
saying I'm gonna win anyway.

00:15:44.990 --> 00:15:46.465
I don't care about Saturn.

00:15:46.465 --> 00:15:47.380
- (laughing)

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:48.213
I love that.

00:15:48.213 --> 00:15:49.046
- I don't care how-

00:15:49.046 --> 00:15:50.006
- Did you say it to the teacher?

00:15:50.006 --> 00:15:52.020
- No. I was, you know,
something I think a lot

00:15:52.020 --> 00:15:54.880
about actually is how bad of a student

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:57.275
I was and how disruptive in class I was

00:15:57.275 --> 00:15:59.650
'cause I was always a little bit

00:15:59.650 --> 00:16:02.124
of a showman in hindsight,
very much a class clown.

00:16:02.124 --> 00:16:05.970
But unbelievably liked by my teachers

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:07.590
for somebody who was disruptive

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:08.580
because I think what I,

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:10.590
the reason I wouldn't say that was

00:16:10.590 --> 00:16:13.612
it's very uncomfortable
for me to be disrespectful.

00:16:13.612 --> 00:16:15.409
- Interesting.

00:16:15.409 --> 00:16:18.339
- So I would play, you know, right?

00:16:18.339 --> 00:16:21.152
I would understand where I
could get away with things

00:16:21.152 --> 00:16:26.152
that would seem like lighthearted or.

00:16:26.242 --> 00:16:28.874
- It sounds like you can completely

00:16:28.874 --> 00:16:30.090
read people's mindset.

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:30.923
- 100%.

00:16:30.923 --> 00:16:32.262
- Yeah.

00:16:32.262 --> 00:16:34.422
And that must be a
massive skill and mindset-

00:16:34.422 --> 00:16:35.255
- It is the skill.

00:16:35.255 --> 00:16:36.950
- Business, yeah.
- It is the skill of life.

00:16:36.950 --> 00:16:37.783
- Yes.

00:16:37.783 --> 00:16:40.544
- If I could wish anybody
anything besides health,

00:16:40.544 --> 00:16:44.520
it would be emotional intelligence.

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:46.260
- Yes, absolutely.

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:48.880
Where do you see yourself
20, 30 years' time?

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:52.180
- You know, I don't think
in those kinds of ways.

00:16:52.180 --> 00:16:57.180
My intuition is a far
more complete, stronger,

00:17:00.746 --> 00:17:05.746
thoughtful version of who I am today.

00:17:07.246 --> 00:17:09.836
With probably a lot more awareness.

00:17:09.836 --> 00:17:12.890
I intuitively have this deep feeling

00:17:12.890 --> 00:17:16.448
that everybody on earth
is gonna know who I am.

00:17:16.448 --> 00:17:17.281
- I absolutely agree.

00:17:17.281 --> 00:17:18.114
- I really do.

00:17:18.114 --> 00:17:19.240
I really do.

00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:22.387
So, you know, probably in
a very interesting place.

00:17:22.387 --> 00:17:25.776
- How, like you've got
the stage ready to go.

00:17:25.776 --> 00:17:28.931
What, if you could say
something to the world

00:17:28.931 --> 00:17:30.691
and raise their happiness,

00:17:30.691 --> 00:17:32.920
what do you think the key thing is?

00:17:32.920 --> 00:17:35.670
- I think giving more than you take

00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:37.283
is an incredible way to get.

00:17:40.020 --> 00:17:41.620
I think that uh,

00:17:41.620 --> 00:17:44.899
I think that karma is practical.

00:17:44.899 --> 00:17:48.520
I think that doing the right thing

00:17:48.520 --> 00:17:49.700
and being the bigger person

00:17:49.700 --> 00:17:52.333
in every situation is always right.

00:17:53.339 --> 00:17:58.339
I think that happiness
is remarkably quiet,

00:17:58.490 --> 00:18:00.700
and negativity is extremely loud.

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:04.110
And so do not allow that to confuse you

00:18:04.110 --> 00:18:05.543
of how great things are.

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:08.770
I think those things stand out to me.

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:10.200
- That's brilliant.

00:18:10.200 --> 00:18:11.798
- Of loud and quiet.

00:18:11.798 --> 00:18:14.494
You know, I think a lot
of people right now,

00:18:14.494 --> 00:18:17.340
you know social media exposes us.

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:18.173
It doesn't change us.

00:18:18.173 --> 00:18:20.120
And what it,

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:21.700
in my true belief that negativity

00:18:21.700 --> 00:18:23.240
is always louder than positivity.

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:24.486
Louder, not truer.

00:18:24.486 --> 00:18:27.160
What you're seeing right now is a lot

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:28.940
of people arguing and complaining

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:30.960
and spitting poison on social.

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:34.080
Yet, the 99% that are silent are actually

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:35.440
in a good place.

00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:37.940
And back to your point
if I had the world stage,

00:18:37.940 --> 00:18:39.589
the reason I would wanna push that

00:18:39.589 --> 00:18:41.911
is I would like to create a call of arms

00:18:41.911 --> 00:18:45.360
of if you're in a good place to share.

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:47.110
Like I'm proud that this morning

00:18:47.110 --> 00:18:48.611
when I was brushing my teeth in Sydney

00:18:48.611 --> 00:18:50.470
I literally looked at my phone,

00:18:50.470 --> 00:18:53.006
it is my framework to think that way,

00:18:53.006 --> 00:18:55.350
and I tweeted a blue heart.

00:18:55.350 --> 00:18:56.261
A blue heart emoji.

00:18:56.261 --> 00:18:57.978
Why blue, I don't know.

00:18:57.978 --> 00:18:59.666
Not necessarily my favorite color.

00:18:59.666 --> 00:19:01.142
I just saw, like.

00:19:01.142 --> 00:19:03.220
- Just sending some love out to the world.

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:04.053
- Actually I do know.

00:19:04.053 --> 00:19:08.640
Subconsciously I think somebody
might have an attachment

00:19:08.640 --> 00:19:09.473
to a blue heart.

00:19:09.473 --> 00:19:11.140
And when they just see it that might,

00:19:11.140 --> 00:19:14.130
if 16 people are effected
by that in a positive way.

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:16.530
And so I think we need a lot more of that.

00:19:16.530 --> 00:19:18.530
Why do we only tweet when we complain

00:19:18.530 --> 00:19:19.620
about an airline?

00:19:19.620 --> 00:19:21.082
How about when you had a lovely flight?

00:19:21.082 --> 00:19:23.873
Why can't be tweet that we
had an incredible stewardess?

00:19:23.873 --> 00:19:24.920
- That's so good.

00:19:24.920 --> 00:19:26.090
- Why don't we do that?

00:19:26.090 --> 00:19:26.923
- Let's do it.

00:19:26.923 --> 00:19:28.960
- And I think we need to
make positivity louder.

00:19:28.960 --> 00:19:29.793
- Absolutely.

00:19:29.793 --> 00:19:31.050
- As a collective.

00:19:31.050 --> 00:19:32.522
- That's what we're on about.

00:19:32.522 --> 00:19:34.110
Tell me, do you have any kind

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:36.335
of spirituality or faith
behind what you do?

00:19:36.335 --> 00:19:37.530
- Not really.

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:38.664
You know it's interesting,

00:19:38.664 --> 00:19:41.790
my family grew up in the Soviet Union.

00:19:41.790 --> 00:19:43.076
And what a lot of people
don't know about communism

00:19:43.076 --> 00:19:46.440
is that religion is outlawed.

00:19:46.440 --> 00:19:47.273
- Really?

00:19:47.273 --> 00:19:49.430
- All religion is outlawed by communism.

00:19:49.430 --> 00:19:52.443
So starting at my great grandfather level

00:19:52.443 --> 00:19:54.875
the majority of my family
never really practiced

00:19:54.875 --> 00:19:56.908
the faith of being Jewish.

00:19:56.908 --> 00:19:59.052
So we are not deeply religious.

00:19:59.052 --> 00:20:01.261
I don't really even,

00:20:01.261 --> 00:20:04.870
you know there is no spiritual guide

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:07.202
or scriptures or books I've read.

00:20:07.202 --> 00:20:12.202
I'm just deeply intuitive
around my humanity and kindness,

00:20:12.497 --> 00:20:15.040
and that's what I follow.

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:16.802
- So you don't necessarily believe in God?

00:20:16.802 --> 00:20:18.032
- You know it's funny,

00:20:18.032 --> 00:20:21.050
I have always and still feel that

00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:22.441
if you ask me that
question I would say I do.

00:20:22.441 --> 00:20:26.840
But I don't really think
of it much more past that.

00:20:26.840 --> 00:20:28.459
And I don't know if I'm checking the box

00:20:28.459 --> 00:20:32.303
because it's a thing to say.

00:20:33.345 --> 00:20:37.992
I will say that I'm
unbelievably cynical to religion

00:20:37.992 --> 00:20:40.520
in the fact that I think a lot

00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:44.320
of it underlining
creates lines in the sand

00:20:44.320 --> 00:20:45.360
to hate others.

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:46.445
- Absolutely.

00:20:46.445 --> 00:20:48.500
- So I think the manifestation

00:20:48.500 --> 00:20:50.802
of modern man and woman of religion

00:20:50.802 --> 00:20:53.558
is something that should be questioned.

00:20:53.558 --> 00:20:55.170
You know it's my great fear right now

00:20:55.170 --> 00:20:57.384
with the rise of nationalism
around the world.

00:20:57.384 --> 00:21:00.280
Anything that says we're Americans

00:21:00.280 --> 00:21:01.230
and screw everybody else,

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:02.673
we're Australians and
screw everybody else.

00:21:02.673 --> 00:21:05.152
We're women and screw everybody else.

00:21:05.152 --> 00:21:08.377
